[[:db/retract 17592186202600 :answer-field/choices 17592186202601] [:db/retract 17592186202600 :answer-field/choices 17592186202602] [:db/retract 17592186202600 :answer-field/choices 17592186202603] [:db/retract 17592186202600 :answer-field/choices 17592186202604] [:db/retract 17592186202600 :answer-field/choices 17592186202605] [:db/retract 17592186202723 :answer-field/choices 17592186202724] [:db/retract 17592186202723 :answer-field/choices 17592186202725] [:db/retract 17592186202723 :answer-field/choices 17592186202726] [:db/retract 17592186202723 :answer-field/choices 17592186202727] [:db/retract 17592186202723 :answer-field/choices 17592186202728] [:db/retract 17592186202607 :answer-field/choices 17592186202608] [:db/retract 17592186202607 :answer-field/choices 17592186202609] [:db/retract 17592186202607 :answer-field/choices 17592186202610] [:db/retract 17592186202607 :answer-field/choices 17592186202611] [:db/retract 17592186202607 :answer-field/choices 17592186202612] {:db/id 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06d00ab5-b798-54f9-9155-cb3b190eccdd" "question-a2d81c89-6939-51ba-b7c7-704655922181" "question-0adf3af5-290b-57ec-82ed-01a980659e66"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203803 :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n\nCalculate $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overline{x}$ and $\\overline{y}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{15+12+13+16+19}{5} = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{8+13+6+15+13}{5} = 11\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the $x_i$ and $\\overline{x}$, $y_i$ and $\\overline{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\, (y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $-3$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-6$ | $10$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n\nTherefore, $S_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = 0 + (-6) + 10 + 4 + 8 = 16.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ac49558f-18ee-5f4d-ae88-d48f8fce7444" "question-5f1ce794-6e38-5896-94a0-a08e42af5009" "question-783f4f6c-a7ae-5188-a502-9fe2f7c3c94b" "question-af73b3f9-9505-5255-a05e-b12a6848bab1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203805 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $35$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{35},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{35}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=35,\\,{S}_{yy}=133,\\,{S}_{xy}=105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\mathrm{Cov}(x, y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that $S_{xy} = 105.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{105}{35} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d18e628f-0f71-500f-a909-b31e50aba9f8" "question-8985aab7-37e2-5eaf-8405-71a24796c1c6" "question-f69f9435-629a-5550-ae7c-8e46c05363dd" "question-42fccfda-10de-5970-a9ed-3564137d6e6d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203806 :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $8$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $14$ | $12$ | $8$ |\n\nGiven that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334,$ calculate $S_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data $x_i$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the $x_i$ data:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i = 10 + 9 + 8 + 8 + 5 = 40.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\nS_{xx} =334 - \\dfrac{1}{5}(40)^2 = 334- 320 = 14.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-91b1cdc3-3a29-5654-81e4-e52f93ca5959" "question-ae961e11-0326-56d9-bf54-b78685d8bc1a" "question-c92a6a30-c262-56d7-be68-e946a5d2130d" "question-8f3d0803-8d23-5ea9-98da-36f1c313a55f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203804 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $30$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{30},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{30}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}=315, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{y}_{i}=278, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=2\\,964.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDetermine $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the statistic $S_{xy}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =2\\,964-\\frac{1}{30}(315)(278) \\\\  & =2\\,964-2\\,919 \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-06d00ab5-b798-54f9-9155-cb3b190eccdd" :question/id #uuid "06d00ab5-b798-54f9-9155-cb3b190eccdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251865" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{123+122+121+120+125+127}{6}=123\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{102+111+110+105+106+108}{6}=107\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $0$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $6$ | $-2$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0+(-4)+(-6)+6+(-2)+4=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f815c63a-5ecf-5ce3-b831-33cde02c9d6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f815c63a-5ecf-5ce3-b831-33cde02c9d6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f815c63a-5ecf-5ce3-b831-33cde02c9d6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" "answer-54378e41-ed6d-55ce-b916-a2913db68958" "answer-4df65b77-c79e-5339-86c9-e224a22ee3ea" "answer-ac149a28-9c82-50cd-93d4-fcc5ab6e1f18" "answer-4e5c58c7-2283-5a41-b325-74cb1fe7e000"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" :answer/id #uuid "2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54378e41-ed6d-55ce-b916-a2913db68958" :answer/id #uuid "54378e41-ed6d-55ce-b916-a2913db68958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4df65b77-c79e-5339-86c9-e224a22ee3ea" :answer/id #uuid "4df65b77-c79e-5339-86c9-e224a22ee3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac149a28-9c82-50cd-93d4-fcc5ab6e1f18" :answer/id #uuid "ac149a28-9c82-50cd-93d4-fcc5ab6e1f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e5c58c7-2283-5a41-b325-74cb1fe7e000" :answer/id #uuid "4e5c58c7-2283-5a41-b325-74cb1fe7e000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a2d81c89-6939-51ba-b7c7-704655922181" :question/id #uuid "a2d81c89-6939-51ba-b7c7-704655922181" :question/math-academy-id "q-251841" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $10$ | $9$ | $6$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $15$ | $21$ | $22$ | $23$ | $26$ | $17$ | $16$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${x}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{x},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{2+3+10+9+6+5+7}{7}=6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $10$ | $9$ | $6$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $15$ | $21$ | $22$ | $23$ | $26$ | $17$ | $16$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-4$ | $-3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\\,$** | $16$ | $9$ | $16$ | $9$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xx}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=16+9+16+9+0+1+1=52.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dcdc1dd0-6dd9-55fc-8f56-4c2c1bfe43f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcdc1dd0-6dd9-55fc-8f56-4c2c1bfe43f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdc1dd0-6dd9-55fc-8f56-4c2c1bfe43f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-75fa1cbb-8b23-5647-9b66-e2abd16dba91" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd1e2e8e-b50d-56ed-b450-33a47d516b05" "answer-02ba762e-68dd-5d26-8285-bcf47017e5d1" "answer-0794d8af-bca9-5a3d-bc61-0e003ff578f8" "answer-75fa1cbb-8b