 | $11$ | $9$ | $12$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $16$ | $14$ | $23$ | $17$ | $15$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-1$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\\,$** | $1$ | $9$ | $36$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{yy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=1+9+36+0+4=50.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202600 :answer-field/correct "answer-1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e91a02b-fc69-5e88-9774-ad00afc6e6ba" "answer-9a918d1e-73e9-5c1c-bc54-cf85f315a090" "answer-b8d3c88f-96c7-55f4-a69d-a68bc5f64a80" "answer-e949b957-3ab5-5b0a-bdc3-5aaf0dc73ccb" "answer-1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e91a02b-fc69-5e88-9774-ad00afc6e6ba" :answer/id #uuid "8e91a02b-fc69-5e88-9774-ad00afc6e6ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a918d1e-73e9-5c1c-bc54-cf85f315a090" :answer/id #uuid "9a918d1e-73e9-5c1c-bc54-cf85f315a090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8d3c88f-96c7-55f4-a69d-a68bc5f64a80" :answer/id #uuid "b8d3c88f-96c7-55f4-a69d-a68bc5f64a80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e949b957-3ab5-5b0a-bdc3-5aaf0dc73ccb" :answer/id #uuid "e949b957-3ab5-5b0a-bdc3-5aaf0dc73ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb" :answer/id #uuid "1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0adf3af5-290b-57ec-82ed-01a980659e66" :question/id #uuid "0adf3af5-290b-57ec-82ed-01a980659e66" :question/math-academy-id "q-251840" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${y}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{y},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{13+15+16+18+14+17}{6}=15.5\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-2.5$ | $-0.5$ | $0.5$ | $2.5$ | $-1.5$ | $1.5$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\\,$** | $6.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $6.25$ | $2.25$ | $2.25$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{yy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=6.25+0.25+0.25+6.25+2.25+2.25=17.5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-644ff868-6cbb-5492-a503-41cd22bf83f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-644ff868-6cbb-5492-a503-41cd22bf83f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "644ff868-6cbb-5492-a503-41cd22bf83f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-306f544b-90da-5c78-b553-0d134db9de1a" "answer-f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" "answer-b8fe5882-4034-5822-be4d-7116344ced62" "answer-afde0403-99c2-50a7-a1c1-6ebf58f5a1c7" "answer-b059aaf0-3095-568d-a33a-3b5bbaa29fd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-306f544b-90da-5c78-b553-0d134db9de1a" :answer/id #uuid "306f544b-90da-5c78-b553-0d134db9de1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=15.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" :answer/id #uuid "f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=17.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8fe5882-4034-5822-be4d-7116344ced62" :answer/id #uuid "b8fe5882-4034-5822-be4d-7116344ced62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=19.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afde0403-99c2-50a7-a1c1-6ebf58f5a1c7" :answer/id #uuid "afde0403-99c2-50a7-a1c1-6ebf58f5a1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=21.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b059aaf0-3095-568d-a33a-3b5bbaa29fd0" :answer/id #uuid "b059aaf0-3095-568d-a33a-3b5bbaa29fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=25.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204443 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $8$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{8},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{8}.$\n\nYou are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}=1.6, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}=5.1, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})=2.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given statistics, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =2.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202599 :answer-field/correct "answer-b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d" :answer/id #uuid "b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204447 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=125,\\,{S}_{yy}=37,\\,{S}_{xy}=64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{xx}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xx}=125.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{125}{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202613 :answer-field/correct "answer-6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa" :answer/id #uuid "6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ac49558f-18ee-5f4d-ae88-d48f8fce7444" :question/id #uuid "ac49558f-18ee-5f4d-ae88-d48f8fce7444" :question/math-academy-id "q-251853" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $36$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{36},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{36}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=72,\\,{S}_{yy}=36,\\,{S}_{xy}=54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{xx}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xx}=72.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{72}{36} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e373ea2c-9a67-56c0-915f-3067e964017d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e373ea2c-9a67-56c0-915f-3067e964017d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e373ea2c-9a67-56c0-915f-3067e964017d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7" :answer/id #uuid "f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f1ce794-6e38-5896-94a0-a08e42af5009" :question/id #uuid "5f1ce794-6e38-5896-94a0-a08e42af5009" :question/math-academy-id "q-251855" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $18$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{18},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{18}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=36,\\,{S}_{yy}=27,\\,{S}_{xy}=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{y}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{y}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{yy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{yy}=27.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{y}^{2} & =\\frac{27}{18} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16c3bebc-0c5b-52e0-b178-4898ba483cba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16c3bebc-0c5b-52e0-b178-4898ba483cba" :answer-field/id #uuid "16c3bebc-0c5b-52e0-b178-4898ba483cba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312" :answer-field/choices ["answer-308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312" :answer/id #uuid "308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-783f4f6c-a7ae-5188-a502-9fe2f7c3c94b" :question/id #uuid "783f4f6c-a7ae-5188-a502-9fe2f7c3c94b" :question/math-academy-id "q-251862" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $16$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{16},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{16}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=188,\\,{S}_{yy}=354,\\,{S}_{xy}=212.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=212.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{212}{16} \\\\  & =13.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-035cd52a-864b-5a48-b335-680aca817a12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-035cd52a-864b-5a48-b335-680aca817a12" :answer-field/id #uuid "035cd52a-864b-5a48-b335-680aca817a12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444" :answer/id #uuid "8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-af73b3f9-9505-5255-a05e-b12a6848bab1" :question/id #uuid "af73b3f9-9505-5255-a05e-b12a6848bab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-251859" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $10$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{10},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{10}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=5,\\,{S}_{yy}=7,\\,{S}_{xy}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=6.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{6}{10} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4924e73-d6d0-52bf-abba-4d9b0890fbd8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4924e73-d6d0-52bf-abba-4d9b0890fbd8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4924e73-d6d0-52bf-abba-4d9b0890fbd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c" :answer/id #uuid "a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d18e628f-0f71-500f-a909-b31e50aba9f8" :question/id #uuid "d18e628f-0f71-500f-a909-b31e50aba9f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-251899" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $9$ | $10$ | $13$ | $11$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $14$ | $14$ | $15$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{y}_{i}^{2}=1\\,186,$ calculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{y}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${y}_{i}$ data:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{y}_{i}=12+13+16+14+14+15=84.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{y}_{i}^{2}=1\\,186.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=1\\,186-\\frac{1}{6}(84)^{2}=1\\,186-1\\,176=10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aa670db5-5eee-5eed-a197-ce090c8f65d9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa670db5-5eee-5eed-a197-ce090c8f65d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa670db5-5ee