 to the following system of equations by eliminating the variable $a:$ \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5a+4b=7 \\\\ -2a+6b=20\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $a$-coefficient in the first equation is $5,$ while in the second equation it is $-2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $5,$ then the $a$-coefficient in the first and second equations will become $10$ and $-10,$ and these will cancel when we add the equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,5a+4b=7\\,)\\,\\times (2) \\\\ (\\,-2a+6b=20\\,)\\,\\times (5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}10a+8b=14 \\\\ -10a+30b=100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{10a}+8b & =14 \\\\ -\\cancel{10a}+30b & =100 \\\\ (8b+30b) & =(14+100) \\\\ 38b & =114 \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b=3.$ However, we still need to find $a.$ To do this, we substitute $b=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a+4b & =7 \\\\ 5a+4(3) & =7 \\\\ 5a+12 & =7 \\\\ 5a & =-5 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-1$ and $b=3,$ which can be written as $(-1,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-21695324-e1d6-52e7-aecd-373a888a2a3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-21695324-e1d6-52e7-aecd-373a888a2a3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "21695324-e1d6-52e7-aecd-373a888a2a3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-01260ea6-923c-58aa-a2e5-5677c1771b2a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01260ea6-923c-58aa-a2e5-5677c1771b2a" "answer-b8c5fa91-1742-5f01-be92-b24c6d9587a5" "answer-90979a4f-f0a4-5329-9332-c50cc5846e88" "answer-652a5ebd-4272-5f28-add3-defc48f2c0b2" "answer-d68c1106-2bb7-5856-b5b7-34531747295e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01260ea6-923c-58aa-a2e5-5677c1771b2a" :answer/id #uuid "01260ea6-923c-58aa-a2e5-5677c1771b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8c5fa91-1742-5f01-be92-b24c6d9587a5" :answer/id #uuid "b8c5fa91-1742-5f01-be92-b24c6d9587a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90979a4f-f0a4-5329-9332-c50cc5846e88" :answer/id #uuid "90979a4f-f0a4-5329-9332-c50cc5846e88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-652a5ebd-4272-5f28-add3-defc48f2c0b2" :answer/id #uuid "652a5ebd-4272-5f28-add3-defc48f2c0b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d68c1106-2bb7-5856-b5b7-34531747295e" :answer/id #uuid "d68c1106-2bb7-5856-b5b7-34531747295e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233460 :question/problem "Given the graph of $y=f(x),$ we apply the following transformations in the order given:\n\n1\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $8$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n2\\. Stretch it by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\n3\\. Translate it to the left by $10$ units\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $8$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $8.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=8f(x).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Stretching the graph of $y=8f(x)$ by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $\\frac{1}{5}x.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=8f(\\frac{1}{5}x)=8f(\\frac{x}{5}).\n  $$\n\n3\\. Translating the graph of $y=8f(\\frac{x}{5})$ by $10$ units to the left is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $(x+10).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=8f(\\frac{1}{5}(x+10))=8f(\\frac{x}{5}+2).\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=8f(\\frac{x}{5}+2).$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffa36a73-cb38-5a3e-b22f-94ae7972e4d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffa36a73-cb38-5a3e-b22f-94ae7972e4d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffa36a73-cb38-5a3e-b22f-94ae7972e4d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c39f5368-56a8-56a6-9249-778f2951044b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce83393b-e04b-54a4-bf3c-968bb6cbc7d7" "answer-b707a1d1-57fa-5736-811f-bf2ae96d060d" "answer-ead58f74-c494-532c-8715-c931593791f3" "answer-c39f5368-56a8-56a6-9249-778f2951044b" "answer-fed01fe7-79b8-5045-81a9-f0e7af4fb8c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce83393b-e04b-54a4-bf3c-968bb6cbc7d7" :answer/id #uuid "ce83393b-e04b-54a4-bf3c-968bb6cbc7d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8f(5x)+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b707a1d1-57fa-5736-811f-bf2ae96d060d" :answer/id #uuid "b707a1d1-57fa-5736-811f-bf2ae96d060d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8f(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ead58f74-c494-532c-8715-c931593791f3" :answer/id #uuid "ead58f74-c494-532c-8715-c931593791f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8f(\\frac{x}{5})+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c39f5368-56a8-56a6-9249-778f2951044b" :answer/id #uuid "c39f5368-56a8-56a6-9249-778f2951044b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8f(\\frac{x}{5}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fed01fe7-79b8-5045-81a9-f0e7af4fb8c6" :answer/id #uuid "fed01fe7-79b8-5045-81a9-f0e7af4fb8c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{8}f(\\frac{x}{5}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233542 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0bc5ff01-f7ae-5810-8e9a-c63f6da9b11b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0bc5ff01-f7ae-5810-8e9a-c63f6da9b11b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc5ff01-f7ae-5810-8e9a-c63f6da9b11b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e6c14c3-46ef-52b6-9c5a-9d55e3141b28" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60e0e66a-c149-588b-90b5-4254cd022492" "answer-68ab3fb9-a119-597e-9344-6ff98a17ba94" "answer-60b74954-3003-503f-a9dc-2f3cea1add5a" "answer-4e6c14c3-46ef-52b6-9c5a-9d55e3141b28" "answer-7e36ff1c-756d-5ab9-a64f-f67db129bbaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60e0e66a-c149-588b-90b5-4254cd022492" :answer/id #uuid "60e0e66a-c149-588b-90b5-4254cd022492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-67-15\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68ab3fb9-a119-597e-9344-6ff98a17ba94" :answer/id #uuid "68ab3fb9-a119-597e-9344-6ff98a17ba94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63+12\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60b74954-3003-503f-a9dc-2f3cea1add5a" :answer/id #uuid "60b74954-3003-503f-a9dc-2f3cea1add5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63+15\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e6c14c3-46ef-52b6-9c5a-9d55e3141b28" :answer/id #uuid "4e6c14c3-46ef-52b6-9c5a-9d55e3141b28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81+15\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e36ff1c-756d-5ab9-a64f-f67db129bbaa" :answer/id #uuid "7e36ff1c-756d-5ab9-a64f-f67db129bbaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81-12\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087692 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a5359436-369e-5935-88c6-73a8053a9364" "question-5f3a9a12-37bd-5534-bce9-24153ef1f5e3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a5359436-369e-5935-88c6-73a8053a9364" :question/id #uuid "a5359436-369e-5935-88c6-73a8053a9364" :question/math-academy-id "q-66526" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}$ as a power of $e$ (the base of the natural logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{1/2}}={e}^{-1/2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{e}})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-1/2})\n$$\n\nThe natural logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-1/2})=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6fd07e78-dd69-5881-8015-dd32bee64dd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6fd07e78-dd69-5881-8015-dd32bee64dd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd07e78-dd69-5881-8015-dd32bee64dd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6042c78b-71af-5276-80cf-ccdcb9284bf0" "answer-6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" "answer-b10534f0-4c95-531e-94d6-ba5e4a60964c" "answer-f7b61c9c-6858-5b2e-a66c-1ae788e691c5" "answer-c6fff638-a832-599c-b20d-b7725b1e8582"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6042c78b-71af-5276-80cf-ccdcb9284bf0" :answer/id #uuid "6042c78b-71af-5276-80cf-ccdcb9284bf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" :answer/id #uuid "6614a67a-a7fe-55e2-be74-7e1ab3c9e3c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b10534f0-4c95-531e-94d6-ba5e4a60964c" :answer/id #uuid "b10534f0-4c95-531e-94d6-ba5e4a60964c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7b61c9c-6858-5b2e-a66c-1ae788e691c5" :answer/id #uuid "f7b61c9c-6858-5b2e-a66c-1ae788e691c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6fff638-a832-599c-b20d-b7725b1e8582" :answer/id #uuid "c6fff638-a832-599c-b20d-b7725b1e8582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233592 :question/problem "![](images/a6/a61a6232b2041bab3d455a7d765311ddfae25f674f8dbbf79696d2137355b159.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram shown above represents two events $A$ and $B$ and the number of outcomes in each region of the sample space.\n\nGiven that every outcome is equally likely, find $P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the probability of an event using a Venn diagram, we count the number of outcomes in the region that represents the event, and divide by the total number of outcomes of the sample space $S.$\n\nIn the Venn diagram, ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}$ is represented by the area outside the circle $B$ or outside the circle $A$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/6a/6a3bb7b671e45aeb15d3239cae6fcedb7c36e52b15141d66b23e65066ab37edc.png)\n\nWe count up the outcomes:\n\n- The number of outcomes in ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\n2+5+1=8\n$$\n\n- The total number of outcomes in $S$ is\n\n$$\n2+9+5+1=17.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=\\frac{8}{17}.\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f94bd53-f137-5cf0-9547-b2c16a22c866"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f94bd53-f137-5cf0-9547-b2c16a22c866" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f94bd53-f137-5cf0-9547-b2c16a22c866" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25d9c9bd-9d1a-5474-8d96-6dd5e36e339b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1537842d-13cc-58e0-a0d1-143d9983a915" "answer-fd4ece7b-d879-59f6-b3c7-36a00c82fb05" "answer-25d9c9bd-9d1a-5474-8d96-6dd5e36e339b" "answer-7dd7ce66-80c6-5c47-a014-bc47fefa20f4" "answer-48992171-11ab-56d9-b3bd-6dc0be5319e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1537842d-13cc-58e0-a0d1-143d9983a915" :answer/id #uuid "1537842d-13cc-58e0-a0d1-143d9983a915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd4ece7b-d879-59f6-b3c7-36a00c82fb05" :answer/id #uuid "fd4ece7b-d879-59f6-b3c7-36a00c82fb05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d9c9bd-9d1a-5474-8d96-6dd5e36e339b" :answer/id #uuid "25d9c9bd-9d1a-5474-8d96-6dd5e36e339b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd7ce66-80c6-5c47-a014-bc47fefa20f4" :answer/id #uuid "7dd7ce66-80c6-5c47-a014-bc47fefa20f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48992171-11ab-56d9-b3bd-6dc0be5319e1" :answer/id #uuid "48992171-11ab-56d9-b3bd-6dc0be5319e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233268 :question/problem "![](images/79/791a76ebbb34751b2ce345243c5de4baf95a32357ce48830e3ea43043011b5e1.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P({X}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P(X)=\\frac{2}{9}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{′}) & =1-P(X) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bbd4dbe8-7797-5473-8b71-522ba839d039"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bbd4dbe8-7797-5473-8b71-522ba839d039" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd4dbe8-7797-5473-8b71-522ba839d039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b237eebf-9c43-59fb-899a-a30b67926304" :answer-field/choices ["answer-522d1120-93d4-5cbb-a277-c571fccf616d" "answer-bfa309f2-83c5-59e0-83a5-90aeb8dbb22a" "answer-a20177b3-3f04-5b8a-9227-27b704dc29d7" "answer-12870f9a-8af7-5922-9f55-72018b822cf6" "answer-b237eebf-9c43-59fb-899a-a30b67926304"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-522d1120-93d4-5cbb-a277-c571fccf616d" :answer/id #uuid "522d1120-93d4-5cbb-a277-c571fccf616d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfa309f2-83c5-59e0-83a5-90aeb8dbb22a" :answer/id #uuid "bfa309f2-83c5-59e0-83a5-90aeb8dbb22a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a20177b3-3f04-5b8a-9227-27b704dc29d7" :answer/id #uuid "a20177b3-3f04-5b8a-9227-27b704dc29d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12870f9a-8af7-5922-9f55-72018b822cf6" :answer/id #uuid "12870f9a-8af7-5922-9f55-72018b822cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b237eebf-9c43-59fb-899a-a30b67926304" :answer/id #uuid "b237eebf-9c43-59fb-899a-a30b67926304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234512 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given equation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{16}^{1/4}=2\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${16}^{1/4}=2$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=2,b=16$ and $x=\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${log}_{16}⁡2=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2c2319c-52ab-5a4c-97b1-53dcd4e20292"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2c2319c-52ab-5a4c-97b1-53dcd4e20292" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2c2319c-52ab-5a4c-97b1-53dcd4e20292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4794e66d-dfd4-5289-9730-730f5a69be16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-239c326a-0a3b-5c29-850c-cac8919a3673" "answer-4779f4c7-29b4-5acc-9108-58e66d5a7ed5" "answer-4794e66d-dfd4-5289-9730-730f5a69be16" "answer-c4e5741e-9798-5186-9c1e-7f4c4d89acfc" "answer-5e21fa3f-1c6c-5a3a-b2e9-4f260f1443e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-239c326a-0a3b-5c29-850c-cac8919a3673" :answer/id #uuid "239c326a-0a3b-5c29-850c-cac8919a3673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{1/4}⁡16=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4779f4c7-29b4-5acc-9108-58e66d5a7ed5" :answer/id #uuid "4779f4c7-29b4-5acc-9108-58e66d5a7ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{1/4}⁡2=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4794e66d-dfd4-5289-9730-730f5a69be16" :answer/id #uuid "4794e66d-dfd4-5289-9730-730f5a69be16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{16}⁡2=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4e5741e-9798-5186-9c1e-7f4c4d89acfc" :answer/id #uuid "c4e5741e-9798-5186-9c1e-7f4c4d89acfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{2}⁡16=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e21fa3f-1c6c-5a3a-b2e9-4f260f1443e2" :answer/id #uuid "5e21fa3f-1c6c-5a3a-b2e9-4f260f1443e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{4}⁡2=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233424 :question/problem "Which of the following expressions are **irrational**?\n\nI. ${8}^{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}$\n\nII. ${3}^{20}\\cdot 7.0523$\n\nIII. $\\sqrt{2}\\cdot {2}^{-15}$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e1969a8-d004-5594-8163-9a16bf27541a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e1969a8-d004-5594-8163-9a16bf27541a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e1969a8-d004-5594-8163-9a16bf27541a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-57e21c9d-b9e5-5edc-bdb6-a68449e17988" :answer-field/choices ["answer-deb59f15-474e-5cf9-aa95-d55b21ee935f" "answer-0250596b-bb74-53f3-9efe-07422f328129" "answer-dfcff7a0-7ab3-58d4-827e-87b601adc05e" "answer-57e21c9d-b9e5-5edc-bdb6-a68449e17988" "answer-8a363189-ada6-5f18-817b-14cb05549c5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-deb59f15-474e-5cf9-aa95-d55b21ee935f" :answer/id #uuid "deb59f15-474e-5cf9-aa95-d55b21ee935f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0250596b-bb74-53f3-9efe-07422f328129" :answer/id #uuid "0250596b-bb74-53f3-9efe-07422f328129" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfcff7a0-7ab3-58d4-827e-87b601adc05e" :answer/id #uuid "dfcff7a0-7ab3-58d4-827e-87b601adc05e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57e21c9d-b9e5-5edc-bdb6-a68449e17988" :answer/id #uuid "57e21c9d-b9e5-5edc-bdb6-a68449e17988" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a363189-ada6-5f18-817b-14cb05549c5e" :answer/id #uuid "8a363189-ada6-5f18-817b-14cb05549c5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-751e0aa2-a931-559b-9a2f-5250360d1346"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-751e0aa2-a931-559b-9a2f-5250360d1346" :question/id #uuid "751e0aa2-a931-559b-9a2f-5250360d1346" :question/math-academy-id "q-118876" :question/problem "A company rents ten identical storage units in the form of a rectangular prism. Each unit is $5\\,\\text{yd}$ long, $3\\,\\text{yd}$ wide, and $3\\text{yd}$ high. If it costs $$2$ per cubic yard per day to rent a storage unit, how much does it cost the company each day to rent the storage units?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one storage unit.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=5,\\,w=3,\\,h=3\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=5\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=45\\,{\\text{yd}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe total volume of the ten units is\n\n$$\n45\\cdot 10=450\\,{\\text{yd}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to rent the storage units, each day the company must pay\n\n$$\n450\\cdot $2=$900.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45a670a5-6eca-551c-9bba-97922b332700"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45a670a5-6eca-551c-9bba-97922b332700" :answer-field/id #uuid "45a670a5-6eca-551c-9bba-97922b332700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2422f0ee-d558-5812-be60-ff74a4a72d4c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05308cdc-72ad-53cb-8842-72a8ffd93c02" "answer-fc5e551c-a4be-5e65-a87d-376cd2db9ece" "answer-d7435a38-2651-52af-beed-87c2b38bfbff" "answer-2fc997cf-68a9-5c5a-a91f-44f31f08abc6" "answer-2422f0ee-d558-5812-be60-ff74a4a72d4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05308cdc-72ad-53cb-8842-72a8ffd93c02" :answer/id #uuid "05308cdc-72ad-53cb-8842-72a8ffd93c02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$400$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc5e551c-a4be-5e65-a87d-376cd2db9ece" :answer/id #uuid "fc5e551c-a4be-5e65-a87d-376cd2db9ece" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$450$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7435a38-2651-52af-beed-87c2b38bfbff" :answer/id #uuid "d7435a38-2651-52af-beed-87c2b38bfbff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fc997cf-68a9-5c5a-a91f-44f31f08abc6" :answer/id #uuid "2fc997cf-68a9-5c5a-a91f-44f31f08abc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$800$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2422f0ee-d558-5812-be60-ff74a4a72d4c" :answer/id #uuid "2422f0ee-d558-5812-be60-ff74a4a72d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$900$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054673 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7f9805c-ce96-515d-891a-332594997042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7f9805c-ce96-515d-891a-332594997042" :question/id #uuid "c7f9805c-ce96-515d-891a-332594997042" :question/math-academy-id "q-85920" :question/problem "A team of $5$ players is to be chosen at random from $7$ boys and $5$ girls.  What is the probability that $2$ boys and $3$ girls will be chosen? Round your answer to the nearest percent." :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ represent the event described in the question. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =\\frac{n}{N},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N$ is the total number of ways to choose $5$ people out of a total of $12,$ and $n$ is the number of picks where $2$ are boys and $3$ are girls.\n\nSince the order in which the players are chosen does not matter, we use combinations.\n\nFirst, we compute $N.$ The number of ways to pick $5$ people from a total of $12$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N={}_{12}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{12!}{5!\\cdot 7!}=792.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $n.$ The computation of $n$ can be divided into two steps: \n\n- the number of ways to choose $2$ (out of $7$) boys is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{7}{C}_{2}=\\frac{7!}{2!\\cdot 5!}=21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the number of ways to choose $3$ (out of $5$) girls is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{5}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{5!}{3!\\cdot 2!}=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the results from the above steps, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n={}_{7}{C}_{2}\\cdot {}_{5}{C}_{3}=21\\cdot 10=210.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =\\frac{210}{792}≈0.27=27%.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3a0c2d2-5b3a-522b-a6d4-7655774ccad3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3a0c2d2-5b3a-522b-a6d4-7655774ccad3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a0c2d2-5b3a-522b-a6d4-7655774ccad3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1ec32d6a-e0a8-5c9e-973c-c722de870f07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-240ee738-741b-5618-af59-6d108f123836" "answer-1ec32d6a-e0a8-5c9e-973c-c722de870f07" "answer-3be7b83f-658e-5186-bf99-aa39df89587a" "answer-40693834-30ab-5f7b-b4a8-410b121d0822" "answer-16176054-57d8-50dd-83a1-0a1e8ea37105"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-240ee738-741b-5618-af59-6d108f123836" :answer/id #uuid "240ee738-741b-5618-af59-6d108f123836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ec32d6a-e0a8-5c9e-973c-c722de870f07" :answer/id #uuid "1ec32d6a-e0a8-5c9e-973c-c722de870f07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3be7b83f-658e-5186-bf99-aa39df89587a" :answer/id #uuid "3be7b83f-658e-5186-bf99-aa39df89587a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40693834-30ab-5f7b-b4a8-410b121d0822" :answer/id #uuid "40693834-30ab-5f7b-b4a8-410b121d0822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16176054-57d8-50dd-83a1-0a1e8ea37105" :answer/id #uuid "16176054-57d8-50dd-83a1-0a1e8ea37105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234270 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c848d579-8366-518a-a3ba-b24a64e2c36d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c848d579-8366-518a-a3ba-b24a64e2c36d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c848d579-8366-518a-a3ba-b24a64e2c36d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fd95737c-f9df-54a0-8ab8-9ef3e07fdf1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd95737c-f9df-54a0-8ab8-9ef3e07fdf1f" "answer-16c23837-9722-5faa-902a-3e9a610ae018" "answer-e9e2076f-e637-5540-becf-7c08397db46e" "answer-389e3585-eb6e-5e0b-b7ad-c87d63aa1f56" "answer-aaef2d17-80ab-59de-9959-f78c7423de66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd95737c-f9df-54a0-8ab8-9ef3e07fdf1f" :answer/id #uuid "fd95737c-f9df-54a0-8ab8-9ef3e07fdf1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t+1}{3t(t+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16c23837-9722-5faa-902a-3e9a610ae018" :answer/id #uuid "16c23837-9722-5faa-902a-3e9a610ae018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4t}{3t(t+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9e2076f-e637-5540-becf-7c08397db46e" :answer/id #uuid "e9e2076f-e637-5540-becf-7c08397db46e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6t+5}{t(t+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-389e3585-eb6e-5e0b-b7ad-c87d63aa1f56" :answer/id #uuid "389e3585-eb6e-5e0b-b7ad-c87d63aa1f56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(t+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaef2d17-80ab-59de-9959-f78c7423de66" :answer/id #uuid "aaef2d17-80ab-59de-9959-f78c7423de66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t+3}{3t(t+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234488 :question/problem "Calculate ${log}_{8}⁡(32)$ without using a calculator." :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8,$ and $X=32.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡(32) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(32)}{{log}_{2}⁡(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{5})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4740df2-7f5f-55f7-996f-1be23039010f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4740df2-7f5f-55f7-996f-1be23039010f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4740df2-7f5f-55f7-996f-1be23039010f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c67bb952-4b1f-5631-b6cd-9cff40172e62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29fbd695-065d-59f9-a978-64ab959589fe" "answer-c582451e-1fd0-5671-8d95-3e20037da447" "answer-154fa8da-d8d4-5d35-a927-4d997f30031e" "answer-22ffff4a-deb5-521a-9391-9c312d39acfd" "answer-c67bb952-4b1f-5631-b6cd-9cff40172e62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29fbd695-065d-59f9-a978-64ab959589fe" :answer/id #uuid "29fbd695-065d-59f9-a978-64ab959589fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c582451e-1fd0-5671-8d95-3e20037da447" :answer/id #uuid "c582451e-1fd0-5671-8d95-3e20037da447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-154fa8da-d8d4-5d35-a927-4d997f30031e" :answer/id #uuid "154fa8da-d8d4-5d35-a927-4d997f30031e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22ffff4a-deb5-521a-9391-9c312d39acfd" :answer/id #uuid "22ffff4a-deb5-521a-9391-9c312d39acfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c67bb952-4b1f-5631-b6cd-9cff40172e62" :answer/id #uuid "c67bb952-4b1f-5631-b6cd-9cff40172e62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186213068 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-18899ab8-1919-5955-a40e-8e20033f8007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-18899ab8-1919-5955-a40e-8e20033f8007" :question/id #uuid "18899ab8-1919-5955-a40e-8e20033f8007" :question/math-academy-id "q-293604" :question/problem "A generator consumes $3$ liters of fuel per hour for the first two hours of use and $5$ liters for each additional hour. Which function $F$ gives the total amount of fuel consumed after $t$ hours, where $t\\ge 2?$" :question/worked-solution "The total amount of fuel consumed consists of two parts.\n\n- For the first $2$ hours, the generator consumes\n\n$$\n3\\times 2=6\\,\\,\\text{liters}.\n$$\n\n- For each additional hour beyond the first $2,$ the generator consumes\n\n$$\n5(t-2)\\,\\,\\text{liters}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total amount of fuel $F$ consumed after $t$ hours, where $t\\ge 2,$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =6+5(t-2) \\\\  & =6+5t-10 \\\\  & =5t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-456409ce-9cbe-59f6-9c9f-5b1ca5269b70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-456409ce-9cbe-59f6-9c9f-5b1ca5269b70" :answer-field/id #uuid "456409ce-9cbe-59f6-9c9f-5b1ca5269b70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7bc7d993-8b07-5c1f-bb87-a59ad81eac7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-043178c1-c125-508a-9bc7-2d3b5ab2bbaf" "answer-c7de47a7-d842-546b-a5f0-ba929b208c17" "answer-dd9abff9-7b86-525c-b8a8-762f29c56795" "answer-be0ba7e5-fe56-50ea-afc4-f6da042055f8" "answer-7bc7d993-8b07-5c1f-bb87-a59ad81eac7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-043178c1-c125-508a-9bc7-2d3b5ab2bbaf" :answer/id #uuid "043178c1-c125-508a-9bc7-2d3b5ab2bbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(t)=3t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7de47a7-d842-546b-a5f0-ba929b208c17" :answer/id #uuid "c7de47a7-d842-546b-a5f0-ba929b208c17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(t)=3t+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd9abff9-7b86-525c-b8a8-762f29c56795" :answer/id #uuid "dd9abff9-7b86-525c-b8a8-762f29c56795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(t)=5t+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be0ba7e5-fe56-50ea-afc4-f6da042055f8" :answer/id #uuid "be0ba7e5-fe56-50ea-afc4-f6da042055f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(t)=5t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bc7d993-8b07-5c1f-bb87-a59ad81eac7f" :answer/id #uuid "7bc7d993-8b07-5c1f-bb87-a59ad81eac7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "F(t)=5t-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233302 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d1c702d-6a7e-53a6-b332-1229b7e63178"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d1c702d-6a7e-53a6-b332-1229b7e63178" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1c702d-6a7e-53a6-b332-1229b7e63178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e93f025c-4fe3-5087-9fca-73eabb8d7f1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86c44bd0-2362-59c6-bcd8-9f87233418ed" "answer-981ccea8-d871-51f5-b71f-5cf2249a16cf" "answer-b180e177-b74d-52e3-b883-4d3735cac1c6" "answer-01e42b42-afd8-540d-8e7d-f99d2145d341" "answer-e93f025c-4fe3-5087-9fca-73eabb8d7f1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86c44bd0-2362-59c6-bcd8-9f87233418ed" :answer/id #uuid "86c44bd0-2362-59c6-bcd8-9f87233418ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{25\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-981ccea8-d871-51f5-b71f-5cf2249a16cf" :answer/id #uuid "981ccea8-d871-51f5-b71f-5cf2249a16cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b180e177-b74d-52e3-b883-4d3735cac1c6" :answer/id #uuid "b180e177-b74d-52e3-b883-4d3735cac1c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01e42b42-afd8-540d-8e7d-f99d2145d341" :answer/id #uuid "01e42b42-afd8-540d-8e7d-f99d2145d341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e93f025c-4fe3-5087-9fca-73eabb8d7f1a" :answer/id #uuid "e93f025c-4fe3-5087-9fca-73eabb8d7f1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186213005 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19e31d5d-5933-52fe-a699-d3240dcd05a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-19e31d5d-5933-52fe-a699-d3240dcd05a2" :question/id #uuid "19e31d5d-5933-52fe-a699-d3240dcd05a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288661" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\n(ax-8)(x+b)=4{x}^{2}-32x+48\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$a+b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ax-8)(x+b) & =a{x}^{2}+abx-8x-8b \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}+(ab-8)x-8b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+(ab-8)x-8b=4{x}^{2}-32x+48.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\na=4.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n-8\\cdot b=48⇒b=-6.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $a=4$ and $b=-6$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ab-8 & =4\\cdot (-6)-8 \\\\  & =-24-8 \\\\  & =-32\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $a+b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =4+(-6) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9df0f739-7e6e-51a0-aeca-cefca94dcd0f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9df0f739-7e6e-51a0-aeca-cefca94dcd0f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9df0f739-7e6e-51a0-aeca-cefca94dcd0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7e944915-2fc2-5b59-b074-8518099067d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e944915-2fc2-5b59-b074-8518099067d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e944915-2fc2-5b59-b074-8518099067d4" :answer/id #uuid "7e944915-2fc2-5b59-b074-8518099067d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233432 :question/problem "![](images/ce/cec25c6ab182494771824bae8c2182bf38b57e2d1e81d913e3e49916c8cc3d60.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=8,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=8$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates  this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/0b/0bb186e7b1c1923e7e8b2776b202b1dcd9b930c56583199964e47530805d246d.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a743042b-63eb-545c-bdc0-1aab409141d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a743042b-63eb-545c-bdc0-1aab409141d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a743042b-63eb-545c-bdc0-1aab409141d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-01dedd08-ded8-5ff9-8bc9-adeb91c83949" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8627579e-91b5-5b56-a03e-7f43967fceb6" "answer-01dedd08-ded8-5ff9-8bc9-adeb91c83949" "answer-904444cb-2f64-5eb5-9c3b-5a0b71fe680b" "answer-7b5cec74-241f-5ece-ab07-506d78ba15ed" "answer-ce895cca-e4ca-58bc-9b7e-d4816e68a767"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8627579e-91b5-5b56-a03e-7f43967fceb6" :answer/id #uuid "8627579e-91b5-5b56-a03e-7f43967fceb6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01dedd08-ded8-5ff9-8bc9-adeb91c83949" :answer/id #uuid "01dedd08-ded8-5ff9-8bc9-adeb91c83949" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-904444cb-2f64-5eb5-9c3b-5a0b71fe680b" :answer/id #uuid "904444cb-2f64-5eb5-9c3b-5a0b71fe680b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b5cec74-241f-5ece-ab07-506d78ba15ed" :answer/id #uuid "7b5cec74-241f-5ece-ab07-506d78ba15ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce895cca-e4ca-58bc-9b7e-d4816e68a767" :answer/id #uuid "ce895cca-e4ca-58bc-9b7e-d4816e68a767" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233127 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dad8af52-393d-59fb-9aa5-60a735e10995"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dad8af52-393d-59fb-9aa5-60a735e10995" :answer-field/id #uuid "dad8af52-393d-59fb-9aa5-60a735e10995" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-67ecaaff-b5ce-51b3-be70-8f364b613256" :answer-field/choices ["answer-67ecaaff-b5ce-51b3-be70-8f364b613256" "answer-ce809b8c-cf9f-5070-93bf-43fcbbf62d4c" "answer-52eb9b6f-e01b-50c8-b9fa-d34b7c6dd065" "answer-27d29f52-682d-5808-8c39-f39fbedb67a2" "answer-8f4e3141-8e03-58a8-8021-4244dbdf124f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67ecaaff-b5ce-51b3-be70-8f364b613256" :answer/id #uuid "67ecaaff-b5ce-51b3-be70-8f364b613256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce809b8c-cf9f-5070-93bf-43fcbbf62d4c" :answer/id #uuid "ce809b8c-cf9f-5070-93bf-43fcbbf62d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=-2" :db/