-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3148c07-b30e-5ef9-a7ce-98aeae65443e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3148c07-b30e-5ef9-a7ce-98aeae65443e" "answer-e559e8d5-044b-536f-be6b-c537f919870e" "answer-5e08de2a-a2d3-5bb5-9eff-7650cc85dd48" "answer-95a56734-4623-5a29-823a-2dcc5eb112ee" "answer-dd724d2d-9deb-58d6-b8f5-0793d0b3ea1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3148c07-b30e-5ef9-a7ce-98aeae65443e" :answer/id #uuid "a3148c07-b30e-5ef9-a7ce-98aeae65443e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e559e8d5-044b-536f-be6b-c537f919870e" :answer/id #uuid "e559e8d5-044b-536f-be6b-c537f919870e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e08de2a-a2d3-5bb5-9eff-7650cc85dd48" :answer/id #uuid "5e08de2a-a2d3-5bb5-9eff-7650cc85dd48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95a56734-4623-5a29-823a-2dcc5eb112ee" :answer/id #uuid "95a56734-4623-5a29-823a-2dcc5eb112ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd724d2d-9deb-58d6-b8f5-0793d0b3ea1c" :answer/id #uuid "dd724d2d-9deb-58d6-b8f5-0793d0b3ea1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119753 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7e50efe9-568f-54f5-835e-03a6e09d3518"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233937 :question/worked-solution "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis. Let us call ${\\theta }^{′}$ the angle that is formed with the $x$-axis such that ${\\theta }^{′}+\\theta =2\\pi $\n\n![](images/eb/eb659af0765e200333ca35b716772d92765c7f46ccc4b267243b3c82ba88a1e8.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }^{′}=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n{\\theta }^{′}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using $\\theta +{\\theta }^{′}=2\\pi ,$ we get $\\theta =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9707ee33-50e5-5d83-8659-e34d49a8a2a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9707ee33-50e5-5d83-8659-e34d49a8a2a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "9707ee33-50e5-5d83-8659-e34d49a8a2a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4fd2d8ba-3ba8-5ea6-a35d-4969c52ff9ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64f794dc-e2dc-5758-ad2d-f07b9dd4ce38" "answer-cefdb48d-3425-56ca-aa9f-081a9420b77e" "answer-4fd2d8ba-3ba8-5ea6-a35d-4969c52ff9ec" "answer-fb1ded3b-66b2-5d93-9cde-d2879d7ff545" "answer-531e8eab-af68-5079-9c20-857bd006a3f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64f794dc-e2dc-5758-ad2d-f07b9dd4ce38" :answer/id #uuid "64f794dc-e2dc-5758-ad2d-f07b9dd4ce38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cefdb48d-3425-56ca-aa9f-081a9420b77e" :answer/id #uuid "cefdb48d-3425-56ca-aa9f-081a9420b77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fd2d8ba-3ba8-5ea6-a35d-4969c52ff9ec" :answer/id #uuid "4fd2d8ba-3ba8-5ea6-a35d-4969c52ff9ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1ded3b-66b2-5d93-9cde-d2879d7ff545" :answer/id #uuid "fb1ded3b-66b2-5d93-9cde-d2879d7ff545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-531e8eab-af68-5079-9c20-857bd006a3f6" :answer/id #uuid "531e8eab-af68-5079-9c20-857bd006a3f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100953 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-124cf999-fb4b-5e99-b208-917f67eaa2a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-124cf999-fb4b-5e99-b208-917f67eaa2a5" :question/id #uuid "124cf999-fb4b-5e99-b208-917f67eaa2a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-100106" :question/problem "![](images/51/51b119021be889ff440ec31d901187c3ee9072a507336a8e1a1854f729f2734f.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2f(x)}{3{x}^{2}}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2f(x)}{3{x}^{2}}=\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 1}(-2f(x))}{{lim}_{x\\to 1}3{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=6.$ Calculating the limits of the numerator and denominator separately, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}(-2f(x))=-2(6)=-12\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}3{x}^{2}=3(1)^{2}=3.\n$$\n\nTaking the quotient of these limits, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2f(x)}{3{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 1}(-2f(x))}{{lim}_{x\\to 1}3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12}{3} \\\\  & =-4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2bbc0ee1-4baa-5173-b100-20018e22dddd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bbc0ee1-4baa-5173-b100-20018e22dddd" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbc0ee1-4baa-5173-b100-20018e22dddd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af41f8b5-15e8-542f-a34e-a6719d2beff7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d889c6b3-3044-5c76-99b3-2a2642944a85" "answer-853dd5cc-daab-5ece-ae95-a298d6f2b256" "answer-af41f8b5-15e8-542f-a34e-a6719d2beff7" "answer-a3e18d71-cbfe-5d8e-b389-7dcd1319d736" "answer-6479f131-e0ca-5c92-beb1-5b91498b7dc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d889c6b3-3044-5c76-99b3-2a2642944a85" :answer/id #uuid "d889c6b3-3044-5c76-99b3-2a2642944a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-853dd5cc-daab-5ece-ae95-a298d6f2b256" :a